PVD("kiribati_ndp_2020-2023",{"docs":["","Kiribati_Development_Plan_2020 2023"],"s":{"1":[[1,"43","4","Cultural Industry Enhancement and Promotion","the Government acknowledges the need to enhance and promote the cultural industry to enrich the tourism experience and generate further employment opportunities.",""],[1,"43","9","Tourism Niche Products Development and Promotion","To develop and promote tourism niche products;",""],[1,"43","12","Tourism Accommodation and Service Standards Upgrade","Upgrade standards of accommodation, restaurants and tour services;",""],[1,"43","14","Tourism Marketing and Promotion Campaign","Tourism campaign and awareness through tourism marketing and promotion.",""],[1,"44","6","Product Diversification for Export Promotion","Through product diversification strategies, the Government plans to increase the export of locally made products including value-added products.",""],[1,"45","3","Product Development and Diversification for Trade and Private Sector Development","The Government seeks to develop inclusive and sustainable trade and private sector development through the promotion of product development and diversification through value adding;",""],[1,"46","5","Business Regulation Improvement Initiative","Increase the country's rankings in the 10 areas of business regulation (as per the EDB index);",""],[1,"46","7","Investment Policy Framework Implementation","iii. Implement an investment policy framework; and",""],[1,"51","6","Sustainable Tourism and Cultural Industry Development","Promote and strengthen sustainable tourism and cultural industry development",""],[1,"51","11","Product Development and Diversification through Value Addition","Promote product development and diversification through value addittion",""]],"2":[[1,"5","10","Civil Servant Investment and Advanced Training","This plan recognises the importance of investing in our civil servants for they are drivers to the economic growth and development of our country.",""],[1,"26","12","Civil Servant Capacity Building","Unlike past KDPs, this Plan also covers the important issue of capacity building of civil servants.",""],[1,"26","15","Civil Servant Training for Improved Service Delivery","civil servants are able to access training to improve the delivery of their day-to-day jobs.",""],[1,"35","11","Civil Service Skills Upgrading and Expansion Programme","The final component of human resource development is the need to develop civil servants in Kiribati by upgrading and widening their skills.",""],[1,"35","13","Human Resource Development Policy Review and Training Demand Database Update","Reviewing the country's Human Resource Development Policy to better determine the demand for training against the supply (and updating the database);",""]],"3":[[1,"46","3","Commercial Land Reclamation and Allocation Plan","this Government has a long-term plan to address this issue, such as reclamation and allocation of land for commercial uses, through general land use planning.",""],[1,"46","8","Commercial Land Reclamation Investment","Undertake additional investment to increase the land area available for commercial purposes through land reclamation.",""],[1,"69","15","Court-Based Boundary and Eviction Dispute Resolution","Conflicts in relation to boundaries and evictions are settled through the Courts and enforcement is undertaken by the Police department.",""],[1,"69","16","Kiribati Land Information System Improvement and Boundary Survey Programme","The solution to reducing continuous disputes lies in improving the Kiribati Land Information System (KLIS), a data management system, and surveys to determine boundaries.",""],[1,"70","2","Coastal Survey and GIS Recording Capacity Strengthening","the Government plans to strengthen its capacity to ensure that proper surveys are conducted at the coastal level and incorporated in GIS records to capture information on coastal change.",""],[1,"70","8","Central Land Board Capacity Building","Strengthening the Central Land Board by training and capacity building staff;",""],[1,"70","9","Island Land Master Planning and Land Occupancy Management","Developing and managing a Land Master Plan for each island and limiting land occupancy on South Tarawa and Betio to allow for adequate land usage for commercial, industrial residential and open space;",""],[1,"70","11","Land Tenure Management and KLIS Database Maintenance","Improving land tenure management and maintaining the KLIS database for land boundaries;",""],[1,"70","20","Land Reclamation and Resettlement Plan","the Government has proposed three areas for land reclamation in South Tarawa and Betio, as well as a resettlement plan to raise land by two meters.",""]],"4":[[1,"6","6","Global Climate Finance and Assistance Access Expansion","Increasing access to global funds and assistance;",""],[1,"16","3","KDP Implementation and Priority Support Mobilization","Motivate ourselves and our teams to fully implement the KDP and support the priorities of the KDP;",""],[1,"19","10","DIME Taskforce Progress Monitoring Mechanism","Beyond the Plan's launch, the taskforce will meet on a six-monthly basis to measure the progress of each Ministry /Department against the list of indicators spelt out in the KDP.",""],[1,"20","2","National Development Plan Framework Development and Capacity Strengthening","The TA's role included: (i) developing the framework for the KDP; (ii) peer review of a Zero Draft produced by NEPO; and (iii) strengthening the capacity of NEPO staff towards the completion of the Plan.",""],[1,"20","18","Voluntary National Review and Reporting Update Support","The work of the combined three agencies will facilitate updates of the Voluntary National Review (VNR) and other national and international reporting",""],[1,"22","17","Transformational Change Reform Programme","Transformational change will be driven through the KDP and implemented through a programme of reforms at each Ministry.",""],[1,"22","17","Inter-Ministerial Skills and Knowledge Sharing Initiative","The Ministry of Finance and Economic Development (MFED), through NEPO, initiated this programme of transformational change during the formulation of this new Plan by sharing the skills and knowledge with other Ministries and Departments.","Ministry of Finance and Economic Development (MFED)"],[1,"22","18","DIME Taskforce Monitoring and Reporting Mechanism","Members of the DIME Taskforce will be responsible for measuring the Ministries' and Departments' progress and reporting on this to the Development Coordinating Committee (DCC) and onwards to Cabinet and Parliament.",""],[1,"23","2","Development Partner Alignment and Donor Project Analysis","Strengthen the alignment of development partners' participation to the priorities of the new KDP.",""],[1,"23","3","Development Partner Coordination through NEPO Contact Point","Improve the collaboration between development partners and the Government by clearly specifying that NEPO is the contact point and should be consulted early when new projects are discussed with line Ministries.",""],[1,"23","4","High-Level Oversight of Development Partner Projects","Strengthen high level oversight of development partners' projects.",""],[1,"23","5","Government of Kiribati Donor Committee","Strengthen the collaboration between the Government and development partners through the establishment of a Government of Kiribati Donor Committee.",""],[1,"23","7","Integration of Planning and Budgeting","Integrating planning with budgeting is an exciting new area for NEPO and will greatly enhance the timely monitoring of the new KDP.",""],[1,"23","10","Budget Bid Alignment Requirement","When bidding for budget resources above the baseline, Ministries will be required to show how their bids are linked to the KDP priorities;",""],[1,"23","13","Project Alignment Requirement for KDP Priorities","All projects submitted to NEPO must include an explanation of how they will contribute to KDP priorities;",""],[1,"23","15","Annual KDP Performance Reporting","NEPO will prepare a report on the KDP, and its performance, as part of annual budgeting processes.",""],[1,"23","16","Integrated Budgeting and Planning for KDP Mainstreaming","Integrating budgeting and planning will mainstream the new KDP across the whole of Government which will facilitate its implementation and monitoring.",""],[1,"23","17","KDP Mainstreaming in Government Planning","Mainstreaming the KDP in this way means it will become the focal and reference point in the development of Government policies, strategies, programmes and projects.",""],[1,"23","19","Medium-Term Resource Envelope Framework","MFED intends to build a framework for a medium-term resource envelope to match the strategic priorities in the KDP.","MFED"],[1,"23","21","Medium-Term Resource Allocation to KDP Priority Areas","Playing a more active role in allocating resources over the medium term to the KDP priority areas;",""],[1,"23","22","KDP-Aligned Project Approval Reform","Assigning more weight to the KDP alignment in approving projects;",""],[1,"50","7","Partnerships to Mobilize Financing for KDP Implementation","The Government of Kiribati also recognises the value of durable and genuine partnerships to maximise the range of available financing mechanisms to support the full implementation of this KDP.",""],[1,"52","19","External Finance and Aid Coordination Improvement","Increase access, coordination and management of external finance and aid to improve aid effectiveness",""],[1,"67","3","Strategic Planning and Resource Mobilization Strengthening","The time has come to communicate our strategic direction more precisely, to strengthen institutional, human resources, and budget planning, promote more collaborative dialogue with development partners, and promote private sector investment.",""],[1,"102","7","KPA Narrative Proofreading and KPI Alignment Exercise","Proof reading and updating of KPA narrative; alignment of final KPIs to KV20, Manifesto and 2030 Agenda; closing gaps (especially for inactive Ministries); finalisation of Draft",""],[1,"102","10","Knowledge Sharing and Plan Ownership Support","NEPO shared knowledge, skills and understanding on different areas with the DIME Taskforce to help move the Plan forward and take ownership of the new KDP.",""],[1,"103","2","Kiribati Development Plan Formulation and Indicator Alignment","Facilitate the formation of the new Kiribati Development Plan (KDP), review past progress for all national documents against regional and international agendas and align all indicators (national and international) in parallel to the new KDP.",""],[1,"103","3","Unified Reporting Table for National Plan and Regional Commitment M&E","Ensure the formation of the unified reporting table for the Monitoring and Evaluation (M&E) of national plans and regional commitments.",""],[1,"103","4","Single Reporting Process for Framework Reporting Requirements","Ensure the reporting requirements under the following frameworks are met, with a preference for a single reporting process:",""],[1,"103","9","Inclusive Stakeholder Engagement in National Planning and Evaluation","Ensure national planning and evaluation processes include feature inclusive and comprehensive stakeholder engagement.",""],[1,"103","12","Taskforce Consultation and Document Update Process","Each representative (at a level similar to a Deputy Secretary or as per the Senior Responsible Officer's nomination) will present the view of both the Ministry/Agency and the taskforce during these meetings while sourcing all feedback relevant to update the documents.",""],[1,"103","16","Dataset Collection Coordination Support","Assisting in the coordination of dataset collection.",""],[1,"103","17","DIME Taskforce Strengthening for Monitoring and Reporting","The aim of the taskforce is to improve on past gaps (i.e., poor M&E) for efficient and effective future Voluntary National Reviews (VNRs) and other reporting as needed/requested.",""],[1,"104","3","KDP Mid-Term Review and SDG VNR Review and Commenting Process","Reviewing and providing comments on the KDP Mid-Term Review and SDG VNR;",""],[1,"104","7","Development Coordination Committee Monitoring and Evaluation Mechanism","It will have a six-monthly meeting for the purposes of M&E and provide regular updates to the Secretary to Cabinet, Secretary of Finance and OB and any other interested parties.",""],[1,"104","7","Development Indicators Monitoring and Evaluation Review Process","The Development Coordination Committee (DCC) will review any work of the Development Indicators Monitoring and Evaluation (DIME) Taskforce and National Economic Planning Office/National Statistics Office before being tabled at Cabinet by Honorable Minister for Finance and Economic Development/Honorable Vice President.",""],[1,"104","8","National Indicator Alignment Initiative","Align all national indicators, to address fragmentation issues.",""],[1,"104","12","DIME Taskforce Performance Monitoring Mechanism","The plan is that we will continue the momentum of this technical working group, the DIME Taskforce, to monitor respective Ministries' performance (MSPs and MOPs) over the years through six-monthly meetings or through special meetings for urgent requested updates from Cabinet.",""],[1,"104","13","DIME Taskforce for KDP/KV20 Monitoring and Reporting","The intention behind the establishment of the DIME Taskforce is to continue the momentum of this work, so our progress is continuously updated, and we know where we stand.",""],[1,"104","14","Ministry and Agency Progress Oversight Taskforce","The taskforce will oversee the progress of each Ministry/Agency against the list of key activities in the national documents to see how they progress over time.",""],[1,"104","15","Six-Monthly Ministry KPI Ranking and Reporting System","The taskforce will rank the Ministry by their KPI achievements on a six-monthly basis to DCC and Cabinet.","Ministry | DCC | Cabinet"]],"5":[[1,"6","7","Anti-Corruption Legal and Regulatory Strengthening","The Government of Kiribati aims for a corrupt-free society through the strengthening its legislative and regulatory frameworks and the enforcement of and compliance to such frameworks.",""],[1,"6","7","Institutional Independence Enhancement for Good Governance","This also includes enhancing institutional independence to promote good governance and eliminate corruption.",""],[1,"74","4","Anti-Corruption Legal and Regulatory Strengthening","The Government of Kiribati aims for a corrupt-free society through the strengthening of its legislative and regulatory frameworks and the enforcement of and compliance to such frameworks, which also includes enhancing institutional independence to promote good governance and eliminate corruption.",""],[1,"74","5","Leadership Commission Establishment","The establishment of the Leadership Commission (LC) in 2018, following the passing of the Leaders Code of Conduct in 2016, has been a notable addition to our country's National Anti-Corruption Strategy.",""],[1,"74","7","National Anti-Corruption Mechanisms","Te leniwa Vision corroborates Kiribati's commitment to these ideals through its efforts and aspirations to unify the nation and to ensure that all anti-corruption mechanisms are in place at the national level.",""],[1,"74","8","Strengthen Good Governance and Anti-Corruption Mechanisms","The challenges pose by situations such as the COVID-19 pandemic, and their adverse impacts, require collaborative national efforts to maintain and strengthen existing platforms of robust good governance and anti-corruption mechanisms.",""],[1,"74","10","Anti-Corruption Preparedness Strengthening","The Government of Kiribati needs to be vigilant and take necessary steps to strengthen its preparedness programmes, existing mechanisms, legislation and institutions to prevent the risks of corrupt practices.",""],[1,"74","11","Governance Strengthening Initiative","This KDP is aimed at strengthening governance at all levels of the community and the public sector.",""],[1,"74","12","Governance Strengthening Initiative","Stronger governance will help deliver our vision of a wealthy, healthy and peaceful nation for the sake of today's citizens and future generations.",""],[1,"76","14","Timely Financial and Performance Audits","Timely financial and performance audits of Ministries and SOEs undertaken by the Kiribati Audit Office (KAO).","Kiribati Audit Office (KAO)"],[1,"77","2","Institutional and Legal Accountability Mechanisms","it is essential that stringent institutional and legal mechanisms are in place.",""],[1,"80","1","Public Accounts Committee Oversight Strengthening","The review of the roles of the PAC, its membership and independence must be undertaken in this KDP period.",""],[1,"80","2","Kiribati Audit Office Capacity Strengthening","The capacity of the KAO must be strengthened to better fulfill its mandate.",""],[1,"80","4","Regular Audit Follow-Up and Accountability Mechanism","Frequent and regular follow ups on audit reports will assist with the implementation of audit findings.",""],[1,"80","5","Civil Service Public Finance Compliance Strengthening","The compliance of the civil service in its use of public funds to Kiribati's financial laws and regulation must be strengthened.",""],[1,"80","12","Anti-Corruption Legal and Enforcement Reform","The Government must strengthen existing mechanisms to correct corrupt practices of leader(s) through the review, enactment and enforcement of laws including; the Whistleblowers Act, Leaders Code of Conduct, Penal Code and others to ensure accountability and transparency.",""],[1,"82","4","Good Governance and Anti-Corruption Promotion","It is an obligation of the Government to promote and advocate good governance for the betterment of the Kiribati people and to eliminate corruption at all levels through public awareness and prevention.",""]],"6":[[1,"76","8","Religious Bodies Registration Act Review and Implementation","Religious Bodies Registration Act completely reviewed in 2018 and enacted now since Registrar was recently appointed early this year.",""],[1,"76","8","Incorporated Societies Act Finalisation","Incorporated Societies Act is underway and needs further stakeholder consultation to be made and finalised before end of this quarter.",""],[1,"76","11","Implementation and Reporting of Ratified International Conventions","Implementation and reporting of Kiribati's obligations under ratified international conventions.",""],[1,"80","12","International Obligations Compliance and Enforcement","This includes the implementation of international laws within the context of compliance and enforcement by ensuring international obligations are upheld and implemented at the national level.",""]],"7":[[1,"19","7","Tax Compliance and Economic Activity Enhancement","Raising tax compliance and increasing economic activity are solutions, as is working collaboratively with development partners to increase the funding envelope.",""],[1,"19","7","Public Spending Prioritisation for Value for Money","We must also strengthen and prioritise our spending to areas to maximise value for money.",""],[1,"40","6","Revenue Diversification and Tax Base Expansion","the Government is looking at other options to expand revenue sources from fisheries and marine resources as well as other means such as broadening of the tax revenue base and encouraging payment of dividends by the SOE.",""],[1,"41","6","Taxation and Customs Compliance Improvement Measures","Increased taxation revenue through improvements to the taxation and customs systems particularly through better compliance measures.",""],[1,"41","10","Effective Debt Management Controls","Effective debt management controls.",""],[1,"41","11","RERF Efficient Utilisation and Management Enhancement","Efficient utilisation of the RERF and enhancements in its management.",""],[1,"46","12","Revenue Base Expansion through Existing Plans","Implementing existing plans to expand the revenue base;",""],[1,"46","13","RERF Management Maintenance and Monitoring","Continuously maintaining and updating management of the RERF through regular monitoring of the RERF's asset performance and managers;",""],[1,"47","4","Fiscal Revenue Management and RERF Reform","To maintain fiscal stability, the Government has sought to strengthen the management of existing revenue sources and enhance the management of the RERF through reforms.",""],[1,"48","1","New Tax Scheme Establishment","Establishing new tax schemes;",""],[1,"48","15","RERF Capital and Income Growth Management","There are further plans in place to maintain and increase the value of the RERF based on the objectives of the Fund which is to maximize capital and income growth.",""],[1,"52","3","Revenue Collection Strengthening","Strengthen and improve collection of existing revenue sources",""]],"8":[[1,"3","8","Protection of Rights for Women, Children, and Disadvantaged Groups","We must continue to give our citizens the basic freedoms of speech and association and also promote and protect the rights of women, children and the disadvantaged.",""],[1,"76","7","Community Outreach Programmes on Parenting Skills and Social Support","Endorsement of the implementation plan of the Community Outreach Programmes on Parenting Skills and Social.",""],[1,"76","9","Kiribati National Disability Policy and Action Plan Implementation","Implementation of the plan started early 2020.",""],[1,"77","8","Legal and Policy Review and Update for Inclusion","Reviewing and updating laws, ordinances, and policies to be in line with international laws and inclusive of disabled and vulnerable groups;",""]],"9":[[1,"6","3","Community Health Awareness Programmes","strengthen community awareness programmes on sanitation, neo- natal care, reproductive controls and healthier lifestyles",""],[1,"6","3","Sports Participation Promotion","promote engagement in sport",""],[1,"28","25","National Sport Policy","The establishment, endorsement, and implementation of the National Sport Policy.",""],[1,"59","3","Redesign Community Diabetes Outreach Programmes","To re-examine the reasons that existing tactics and approaches to reducing diabetes have not been effective and redesign community outreach programmes to make them more effective;",""],[1,"61","9","Community Physical Activity Promotion Initiative","By strengthening partnerships with local communities, the Government is focusing on engaging our citizens in physical activities through home gardening and sports.",""],[1,"61","10","Household Home Gardening Promotion","the Ministry of Environment Land and Agriculture Development (MELAD) is promoting home gardening at the household level to improve household members' diets and engage them in physical work.","Ministry of Environment Land and Agriculture Development (MELAD)"],[1,"61","18","Sports Promotion and Strengthening Programme","We aim to increase the promotion and strengthening of sports at all levels",""]],"10":[[1,"6","3","Health Facility and Service Delivery Improvement","improve health care facilities and service delivery",""],[1,"30","18","National Counselling Services Expansion","Developing and implementing counselling services across the country;",""],[1,"54","17","Kiribati Health Sector Programme Implementation","Kiribati Health Sector Programme implementation.",""],[1,"55","14","Health Care Facilities and Service Delivery Improvement","Improve health care facilities and service delivery;",""],[1,"61","4","Health Facility Capacity and Equipment Upgrade","we must strengthen of the capacity of our hospitals and health centres and make improvements to our other facilities, medical equipment, ambulances and MRI scanners.",""]],"11":[[1,"9","6","IENRMP Community-Based Integrated Environment and Natural Resource Co-Management Plan","IENRMP Community Based - Integrated Environment and Natural Resource Co-Management Plan.",""],[1,"67","7","Strengthened Enforcement of Fisheries and Environment Acts","Kiribati must ensure that its fragile and highly vulnerable terrestrial and marine environments is protected and safeguarded through better enforcement of its Fisheries and Environment Acts.",""],[1,"67","8","Monitoring, Control and Surveillance Programme for Fisheries Compliance","Currently, the implementation of Monitoring, Control and Surveillance (MCS) programmes focuses on subsistence fishermen's compliance in relation to undersize fish and fishing bans during closed seasons.",""],[1,"67","9","Integrated Environment and Natural Resources Co-management Plans","the development and implementation of the Integrated Environment & Natural Resources Co-management plans (IENCMPs) in the outer islands.",""],[1,"68","11","Environmental Regulations Review and Finalisation","Review, update and finalise regulations on protected areas, protected species, biosafety and other environment related policies.",""],[1,"68","12","Review and Update of the KNBSAP","Secure resources to undertake a review and update of the KNBSAP (2016-2020) and the Kiribati National Invasive Alien Species Strategic Actions Plan, to align to the KIEP, other related strategic documents and policies, the KDP 2020 - 2023, and the KV20.",""],[1,"68","13","Protected Areas and Protected Species Regulatory Update","Review, update and finalize regulations on protected areas, protected species and other environment related policies and regulations.",""],[1,"68","15","Environmental Protection and Biodiversity Conservation Strengthening","Strengthen environmental protections, conservations, management, sustainability, and resilience building, in relation to sustainable development through an increasing focus on proper management of biodiversity and conservation",""],[1,"68","16","Resourcing of Relevant Authorities for Legislative Enforcement","Proper resourcing of relevant authorities for the effective enforcement of legislation;",""],[1,"68","17","Disaster Risk Management and Climate Change Act Enforcement and Implementation","Strengthen the enforcement and implementation of the Disaster Risks Management and Climate Change Act and Environment Act;",""],[1,"68","18","National Capacity Strengthening for Integrated Vulnerability Assessments","Strengthen national capacity in relation to Integrated Vulnerability Assessments (IVAs);",""],[1,"68","19","Strengthening the Civil Service Secretariat for Environmental Impact Assessment Delivery","Strengthen the CSS, including the delivery of Environment Impact Assessment (EIAs), in relation to all development projects;",""],[1,"69","8","Marine Species Restocking Programme","the Kiribati Fisheries Division will focus on restocking programmes in relation to islands facing overexploitation in marine species like seashells and sea cucumbers.",""]],"12":[[1,"42","14","Fisheries Economic and Marine Habitat Evaluation","Promoting the evaluation of fisheries economic values and ecosystems of selected marine habitats;",""],[1,"42","15","Vessel Day Scheme","Maximising economic returns from marine resources and sustainable fisheries development in the pursuit of: i) Vessel Day Scheme;",""],[1,"42","15","Marine Bonded Warehouse","Maximising economic returns from marine resources and sustainable fisheries development in the pursuit of: ii) Marine Bonded Warehouse;",""],[1,"42","15","Purse Seine Net Mending Yard","Maximising economic returns from marine resources and sustainable fisheries development in the pursuit of: iii) Purse Seine Net Mending Yard;",""],[1,"42","15","Marine Stewardship Council Certification","Maximising economic returns from marine resources and sustainable fisheries development in the pursuit of: iv) Marine Stewardship Council Certification;",""],[1,"42","16","Sustainable Livelihoods Support for Artisanal and Small-Scale Fishers","Providing support to maximise sustainable livelihoods of artisanal and small-scale fishers;",""],[1,"42","17","Aquatic Resources Culture and MCS Scheme Strengthening","Promoting and strengthening the culture of aquatic resources and the Monitoring, Control and Surveillance (MCS) schemes and promoting diversification of sustainable and adaptive fishing schemes;",""]],"13":[[1,"70","16","Intangible Cultural Heritage Preservation and Promotion","Collecting, documenting protecting and promoting intangible cultural heritage;",""],[1,"70","18","Public Awareness on Culture, Resilience, and Livelihoods","Raising public awareness designed to demonstrate the significant contribution that culture has on strengthening resilience and supporting livelihoods;",""]],"14":[[1,"6","10","Safe Drinking Water and Basic Sanitation Provision","provision of safe drinking water and access to good basic sanitation",""],[1,"39","2","South Tarawa Water Supply Project","the implementation of new and on-going infrastructure projects such as the South Tarawa Water Supply Project and the Rehabilitation of Primary Schools among others have also contributed to this growth pattern.",""],[1,"86","7","Safe Drinking Water and Basic Sanitation Provision","Provision of safe drinking water and access to good basic sanitation;",""],[1,"89","7","Expansion of Drinking Water and Sanitation Projects","The Government will continue to work with its development partners to expand the scope of ongoing projects and implement new activities to achieve its drinking water and sanitation targets.",""],[1,"89","11","Sanitation Improvement Projects","Various projects have been implemented to improve sanitation in Kiribati, ranging from assessments, school and community awareness programmes, construction of communal and public toilets and the development of a sanitation roadmap addendum 2021-2040 (under way).",""],[1,"90","2","Water Tank Distribution Expansion","Increase the number of water tanks distributed;",""],[1,"90","3","Desalination and Distillation Plant Expansion","Increase the number of desalination and distillation plants;",""],[1,"90","4","Solar and Hand Water Pump Installation in Vulnerable Areas","Increase the number of solar and hand water pumps installed in vulnerable areas;",""],[1,"90","6","Drought Response Plan Development","Development of a drought response plan;",""],[1,"90","7","Water and Sanitation Awareness and Training Programme","Raising awareness and training on water and sanitation programmes;",""],[1,"90","8","Sanitation Roadmap Development","Development of a sanitation roadmap to determine best solutions to address sanitation issues.",""],[1,"90","9","Sanitation Roadmap Addendum Finalization","Finalization of the sanitation roadmap addendum 2021-2024 to determine best solutions to address sanitation issues",""]],"15":[[1,"86","10","Transport Infrastructure Construction, Upgrading and Maintenance","Build, upgrade and sustain roads, causeways, bridges and runways;",""],[1,"91","11","Outer Islands Infrastructure Investment","To improve the economic opportunities in these islands, a large investment is required to give these islands the same infrastructure as the nation's capital.",""],[1,"91","12","Outer Islands Airport Runway Upgrade Programme","Investment in the upgrade of these runways to a standard design will contribute tremendously to improved air services and more importantly the safety of our nationals.",""],[1,"91","13","Kanton Airfield Enroute Alternate Aerodrome Upgrade","Kanton Airfield will provide an enroute alternate aerodrome to enable an Embraer jet to fly directly to Kiritimati Island.",""],[1,"100","4","Transport Infrastructure Upgrade and Maintenance","To build upgrade and sustain roads, causeways, bridges and runways",""]],"16":[[1,"86","6","Infrastructure Development Programme","the KDP 2020-2023 aims to address infrastructure development in several areas over the next four years to bridge existing gaps and enable our country to move to a higher level of development.",""],[1,"86","8","Building Code Compliance and Asset Maintenance Strategy","Increase compliance with the building code and establish an asset maintenance strategy;",""],[1,"87","4","Kanton Island Infrastructure Technical Support","Provide technical support for the development and improvement of infrastructure on Kanton Island.",""],[1,"90","10","Building Code Revision and Maintenance Planning","Critical to the sustainability of past and new infrastructure developments is revision of the country's Building Code, released in 1990, as well as the establishment and adherence to maintenance plans.",""],[1,"90","11","Preventative Maintenance for Social and Economic Infrastructure","We acknowledge the need for preventative maintenance to ensure serviceability of both social and economic infrastructure and to avoid higher costs of repairing and rebuilding resulting from poor maintenance.",""],[1,"90","16","Building Code Review","Review the Building Code;",""],[1,"90","17","Building Code Compliance Enforcement","Ensure all buildings comply with the Building Code;",""],[1,"90","18","Building Maintenance Planning Requirement","Ensure all buildings have a maintenance plan.",""],[1,"90","19","Resilient Building Infrastructure and Green Construction Improvement","Ensure that resilient building infrastructure and Green Construction are improved.",""]],"17":[[1,"5","11","Curriculum Quality Strengthening","strengthen the quality of relevant curricula that support student's diverse learning opportunities",""],[1,"5","11","Student Enrollment Support","Prepare and support students enrolments at all year levels",""],[1,"5","11","Early Childhood Education Legislative and Operational Support","Foster the development of early childhood education through support for the development of an appropriate legislative framework and the development of supportive operational environment",""],[1,"5","11","Student Performance Assessment Strengthening","Strengthen students' performance assessment",""],[1,"5","11","Inclusive Education Support for Students with Special Needs","Identify students with special needs and support them to receive education in mainstream schools",""],[1,"8","5","Accelerated School Readiness Programme","Accelerated School Readiness Programme",""],[1,"26","1","Free and Compulsory Basic Education","Education is free, and compulsory, in Kiribati for those at primary school (Years 1-6) and junior secondary school (Years 7-9).",""],[1,"26","2","Senior Secondary Examination Progression Requirement","Senior secondary school students (Years 10-13) must successfully complete examinations in Year 12 and 13 to progress onto higher education, whether they be technical training or university.",""],[1,"26","3","Expansion of Free Education to Year 12","the Government is expanding the free education up to Year 12 level.",""],[1,"26","14","Education Access and Inclusive Quality Education Initiative","The country is already working to increase access to education and to provide inclusive and quality education for all citizens.",""],[1,"29","5","Contingency and ICT Plan for Education","This sector also recognized that we are in a COVID era and have supplemented a Contingency and ICT plan that supplements the National Contingency plan and ICT in Education Master plan.",""],[1,"29","12","Transparent Communication and Governance System for Education Support","Establish a transparent communication and governance system, which is inclusive of: (i) reviewing administrative systems to improve the delivery of education support services; and (ii) reviewing gaps in early childhood education as this is the crucial starting point that determines the success of all other levels of education;",""],[1,"29","13","Strengthening the Kiribati Education Management Information System","strengthening the Kiribati Education Management Information System (KEMIS) as a powerful data collection tool, to monitor quality of education and inform policy making.",""],[1,"29","14","Teacher Quality Investment Initiative","To invest in quality teachers, we will:",""],[1,"29","15","Teacher Registration and Human Resources Management Reform","Improve the management of human resources through; (i) applying the national teacher's registration process to the national education system, with compliance in respect to the standards, operations and communication system; (ii) ensuring teachers' salary scales are based on knowledge, skills and, above all, qualifications; and (iii) strengthening the monitoring of teachers' absences.",""],[1,"30","10","Teacher Certification and Payroll Registration System","all registered teachers must be listed under the Government's payroll",""],[1,"30","10","Kiribati Quality Standards Assessment Framework","The Kiribati Quality Standards (KQS) guide the assessments for approval of teachers and preschools or ECCE centres at all levels.",""],[1,"30","15","School Participation and Retention Awareness Programme","Increasing participation and retention rates across all levels through an awareness programme and consultation with communities and parents to promote enrolment and child support;",""],[1,"30","16","Compulsory School Attendance Enforcement","Enforcement of approved Acts and policies making it compulsory to send children to school;",""],[1,"30","17","Interactive Learning Exercises and Activities","Designing interactive exercises and activities for greater engagement of children and teachers;",""],[1,"30","19","Data-Driven Education Equity Monitoring and Promotion","Using data-driven interventions to monitor and promote equity across all levels of education, in all locales, across all major groups such as those with Special Educational Needs and Disabilities (SEND);",""],[1,"30","20","Curriculum Improvement and Education Act Review","Supporting diverse learning opportunities through curriculum improvements, i.e., (i) implementation of the early childhood education (ECE) curriculum; (ii) implementation of skills-based education into national curricula across all stages; and (iii) reviewing and consolidating existing Acts (Education Act, 2013 and ECCD Act 2017) to incorporate the missing tertiary level, while incorporating changes and new approaches.",""],[1,"32","17","Student Performance Improvement Initiative","Continually lifting students' performance at all school levels to ensure it remains at a high standard until the completion of their education",""],[1,"32","18","Remedial Learning Interventions Based on Student Assessment Results","Developing remedial interventions based on students' assessment results (specially to promote literacy and numeracy in lower grades).",""],[1,"33","7","School Clubs and Online Learning Promotion","Promote school clubs and online learning;",""],[1,"33","8","Parental Engagement Programmes","Implement parental engagement programmes designed to promote parent-children participation;",""],[1,"36","4","Curriculum Quality and Relevance Improvement","Strengthen the quality and relevant curricula that support students' diverse learning opportunities.",""],[1,"36","15","Early Childhood Education Legislative and Operational Support","Foster the development of early childhood education through support for the development of an appropriate legislative framework and the development of supportive operational environment",""],[1,"36","18","Student Performance Assessment Strengthening","Strengthen students' performance assessment",""],[1,"37","4","Inclusive Education Support for Students with Special Needs","Identify STUDENTS WITH SPECIAL NEEDS and support them to receive education in mainstream schools",""],[1,"39","2","Rehabilitation of Primary Schools","the implementation of new and on-going infrastructure projects such as the South Tarawa Water Supply Project and the Rehabilitation of Primary Schools among others have also contributed to this growth pattern.",""]],"18":[[1,"5","11","Formal and Informal Training Access Pathways","Strengthening and providing pathways for ease of access to formal and informal training opportunity",""],[1,"5","11","Workforce Qualification and Competency Development","Prepare all professions and the public/private workforce to become qualified, competent, knowledgeable and trusted",""],[1,"26","5","TVET Curriculum Pathway for Early School Leavers","MOE has started developing a curriculum pathway to a TVET program at Certificate I and II levels for early school leavers at Year 10 and above.","MOE"],[1,"26","6","Certificate III Training and Progression Pathways","KIT and MTC provide trainings at Certificate III level.",""],[1,"26","8","Government Scholarship Programme for Selected Fields","with the Government providing scholarships in selected fields.",""],[1,"26","8","Scholarship Bonding Requirement for Return Service","Students on scholarships are bonded to work in Kiribati on completion of their studies.",""],[1,"33","9","Student Loan Support for Post-Secondary Education","Support access to post-secondary (tertiary) education with student loans.",""],[1,"34","3","Awards and Short Courses for Trade and Non-Trade Certificates","KIT offers awards and short courses for trade and non-trade certificates (see Figure 10)15, whereas MTC provides training for our country's seafarers and fishermen.",""],[1,"34","7","Certificate Enrolment Expansion in English and Hospitality","Raising enrolments in the Certificates in English and Hospitality offered through KIT16, because in all overseas jobs one of the main skills required is English proficiency;",""],[1,"34","8","Expanded Intake for Caregiving and Priority Training Needs","Increasing intakes at MTC and KIT in caregiving and other identified needs;",""],[1,"34","9","Higher-Level Technical and Nursing Programme Expansion","Raising the qualification level at KIT for the Trade and Non-Trade Certificate III and above and offering nursing programmes at KNS at an advanced diploma level;",""],[1,"34","11","Hospitality Course Enrollment Expansion at KIT","Increasing enrolments in hospitality courses at KIT over the next four years",""]],"19":[[1,"34","6","Seafarer Officer Training Programme","Training more officers than ordinary seaman, because our seafaring workers are facing strict competition for the same types of jobs from other countries;",""],[1,"35","1","Employment Opportunity Maximization","MEHR, through the Labour Division, is responsible for maximising employment opportunities locally and abroad.","MEHR | Labour Division"],[1,"35","5","Employment Support Services Training Provision","KIT plays a crucial role through its Employment Support Services in providing English, fitness, pre-departure and other trainings in response to employers' demands.",""],[1,"35","6","National Labour Mobility Coordination and Labour Market Database","MEHR also coordinates labour mobility initiatives through its National Labour Mobility Working Group and is establishing a national, centralised labour market database in collaboration with relevant stakeholders to keep record of job seekers as part of supporting its marketing initiatives.","MEHR"],[1,"35","7","Supporting Kiribati Welfare through Labour Mobility Project","Another labour mobility initiative is currently being explored with the Canadian labour market through the project 'Supporting Kiribati Welfare through Labour Mobility'.","MEHR"],[1,"35","9","Job Seeker Registration and Placement Coordination","At the national level, MEHR coordinates the registration of job seekers with existing vacancies in Government ministries and also works closely with employers, including in the private sector, to connect job seekers with potential opportunities.","MEHR"],[1,"37","9","Regional Seasonal Workers Access and Entry Support","Improve access and entry to opportunities for I-Kiribati into the Regional Seasonal Workers (RSE) and Seasonal Workers Programme (SWP).",""],[1,"41","14","Kiribati National Labour Migration Policy Implementation","Implementation of the Kiribati National Labour Migration Policy to increase 100 percent in overseas employment by 2019.",""],[1,"49","3","Overseas Employment Market Expansion Measures","The Government, in line with the objectives of the KV20, is implementing measures to strengthen existing, and secure new, overseas employment markets to allow the local population to access decent employment opportunities abroad.",""],[1,"49","4","National Labour Migration Policy Implementation Support","The vision seeks to support effective implementation of the National Labour Migration Policy to increase the number of overseas workers and create new labour markets.",""],[1,"49","4","Strategic Labour Migration Partnerships","The Government will utilise strategic partnerships for win-win arrangements whereby Kiribati as a labour-sending country is able to cater for the demand in labour-receiving countries.",""],[1,"50","3","Employment Creation and Labour Mobility Schemes","The Government's efforts to create employment in the public and private sector, including labour mobility schemes, are complementary.",""]],"20":[[1,"49","5","Social Protection Expansion for Vulnerable Groups","This commitment has led to the introduction or improvement of social protections to cover the unemployed, elderly citizens and persons with disabilities.",""],[1,"50","1","Support Fund for the Unemployed","the Government introduced a Support Fund for the Unemployed (SFU) to support people who are unable to secure jobs as copra cutters.",""],[1,"50","2","Social Benefit Support for Vulnerable Groups","Vulnerable groups such as people living with disabilities, children whose parents have passed away, also receive social benefit support.",""]],"21":[[1,"6","3","Disease Reduction Initiative","Reduce the incidences of serious diseases",""],[1,"26","20","National COVID-19 Preparedness and Response Plan Enhancement","Kiribati will continue to work closely with its development partners to enhance Kiribati's National COVID-19 Preparedness and Response Plan.",""],[1,"55","5","COVID-19 Vaccination Rollout Plan","the vaccination roll out plan is in place to protect national citizens",""],[1,"55","5","Health Safety Awareness Programmes","increasing safety measures through awareness programs etc; when border opens up",""],[1,"56","2","Community-Based Health Compliance Incentive Measures","Introduce innovative, community-based solutions to incentivize people to do the right things for the sake of our children and grandchildren - these may include charging a penalty to people that disregard health guidelines;",""],[1,"57","4","HIV Eradication Initiative","we aim to totally eradicate HIV by 2022.",""],[1,"57","5","HIV Awareness Programme for High-Risk Groups","The public health service within the Ministry of Health and Medical Services (MHMS) will continue to include HIV in its awareness programmes, paying particular attention to high-risk groups such as seafarers, their spouses and those involved in commercial and transactional sex.","Ministry of Health and Medical Services (MHMS)"],[1,"58","6","Tuberculosis Awareness and Referral Mechanism Programme","Implement a new and more effective awareness programme to address the root causes of TB transmission, decrease the risk of developing TB and find an effective referral mechanism;",""],[1,"58","7","Direct Observed Treatment Coverage Expansion","Promote universal and equitable access through expanding Direct Observed Treatment coverage;",""],[1,"58","8","TB Diagnosis and Treatment Monitoring Capacity Strengthening","Strengthen capacity to diagnose and monitor treatment of TB cases, including drug-resistant TB, TB-HIV and TB- DM; and",""],[1,"58","9","TB Drug Management and MDR-TB Comorbidity Management Strengthening","Strengthen the TB drug management system and programmatic management of MDR-TB, TB-HIV and TB-DM comorbidities.",""],[1,"58","10","Public Hygiene Awareness Campaign","a continuous awareness program to the public on hygiene measures to prevent the spread of the deadly disease should it reaches our shores",""],[1,"58","10","Pandemic Resilience and Vaccination Coverage Approach","The Government believed in a resilient approach towards certain pandemics, by taking full coverage dozes from the Ministry of Health","Ministry of Health"]],"22":[[1,"62","10","Reproductive, Maternal, Newborn, Child and Adolescent Health Improvement","Improve reproductive maternal, newborn, child and adolesent health, Health Promotion and Nutrition.",""]],"23":[[1,"6","6","Climate Change Policy and Joint Implementation Plan Implementation","To increase the rate of implementation of the Kiribati Climate Change Policy and the Kiribati Joint Implementation Plan for Climate Change and Disaster Risk Management (KJIP);",""],[1,"6","6","Education, Training, and Community Awareness Programmes","Mounting education, training and awareness programmes and increasing community participation and engagement;",""],[1,"6","6","Early Warning and Disaster Readiness Strengthening","Strengthening our early warning systems and readiness and responsiveness to disasters and emergencies; linked to Disaster Risk Management (DRM) under common issues;",""],[1,"6","6","Multilateral Environmental Agreement Implementation","Implementing national obligations under Multilateral Environmental Agreements (MEAs) including the United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change (UNFCCC), the Paris Agreement decisions of the UNFCCC Conference of the Parties (COP);",""],[1,"6","6","IPCC Information and Reporting Monitoring","Keeping abreast of Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change (IPCC) information and reports;",""],[1,"65","19","Accelerate Implementation of Climate Change Policy and Joint Implementation Plan","To increase the rate of implementation of the Kiribati Climate Change Policy and the Kiribati Joint Implementation Plan for Climate Change and Disaster Risk Management (KJIP);",""],[1,"66","2","Communication, Education, Training, and Public Awareness Programmes","Mounting formal and informal communication, education, training, and public awareness programmes and increasing community involvement, participation, and engagement at all levels of society;",""],[1,"66","3","Early Warning Systems and Disaster Readiness Strengthening","Strengthening our early warning systems and readiness and responsiveness to disasters and emergencies;",""],[1,"66","5","Implementation of Multilateral Environmental Agreement Obligations","Implementing national obligations under Multilateral Environmental Agreements (MEAs) to which the Government of Kiribati is a State Party to, including the United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change (UNFCCC), the Paris Agreement decisions of the UNFCCC Conference of the Parties (COP); and",""],[1,"66","10","Strengthening and Improving National Resilience Plans","Through its responsible agencies, the Government is therefore prioritising its strategies to focus more on strengthening and improving current national resilience plans to enhance and support sustainable development.",""]],"24":[[1,"6","6","Integrated Environment Policy and Action Plan Implementation","To implement the Kiribati Integrated Environment Policy and related environment strategic action plans, e.g., the Kiribati National Biodiversity Strategies and Actions Plan (KNBSAP) and the Kiribati Waste Management and Resource Recovery Strategy (KWMRRS);",""],[1,"65","14","Waste Recovery and Biogas Facility","Waste recovery facility managed through composting, recycling, scrap waste stockpile to be exported, and biogas system installed.",""],[1,"65","20","Integrated Environmental Policy Review and Implementation","To review, update and implement the Kiribati Integrated Environmental Policy (KIEP) and related environment strategic action plans, e.g. the Kiribati National Biodiversity Strategies and Action Plan (KNBSAP) and the Kiribati Waste Management and Resource Recovery Strategy (KWMRRS).",""],[1,"65","21","Strengthen Implementation of the Integrated Environment Policy and Related Action Plans","To enhance and resourced the implementation of the Kiribati Integrated Environment Policy (KIEP), related environment strategic action plans, e.g., the Kiribati National Biodiversity Strategies and Actions Plan (KNBSAP) and the Kiribati Waste Management and Resource Recovery Strategy (KWMRRS), including the Integrated Environment and Natural Resources Co-Management Plans (IENCMPs).",""],[1,"67","2","Waste and Pollution Response Plan","The KWMRRS presents a long-term plan to effectively respond to the increasing threat from waste and pollution, which is most apparent in Betio, South Tarawa and Kiritimati Island - the main urban centres with high population densities.",""],[1,"67","11","Strengthen Compliance with the Country Safeguard System","there is a need to further protect our environment through greater compliance to our Country Safeguard System (CSS), which comprises policies, practices, legal frameworks and institutions put in place to avoid, reduce or mitigate potentially adverse environmental, economic, and social impacts of development activities.",""],[1,"67","12","Formalization of the CSS within the Environment Licensing System","Currently, the Government is prioritizing the development and formalization of the CSS into the existing Environment Licensing System under the Environment Act.",""],[1,"68","1","Robust Environmental Legal and Policy Framework","there is a need for the formulation of a robust legal framework and policies to ensure that Kiribati's fragile environment is protected, conserved, and sustainably managed from unsustainable and environmentally destructive practices of development activities.",""],[1,"68","10","Resource Mobilization for KIEP and Environment Act Implementation","Leverage and secure resources at the institutional, human resources and programme level to effectively and efficiently implement the Kiribati Integrated Environment Policy (KIEP) and the Environment Act;",""],[1,"68","14","Waste Management, Pollution Control and Resource Recovery Implementation Support","Strengthen waste management, pollution control and resource recovery through resourcing and supporting the implementation of the KWMRRS (2020 - 2030)",""]],"25":[[1,"61","19","Community Food Crop Production Training and Support","To strengthen Kiribati food systems and supply chains, MELAD is focused on increasing training and support for communities in the area of food crop production.","MELAD | Agriculture and Livestock Division"],[1,"69","5","Nutrition and Food Access Improvement Initiative","Through this KDP, the Government aims to ensure that people have access to sufficient, safe and nutritious dietary needs.",""],[1,"69","6","Food Systems and Supply Chain Strengthening","Kiribati strengthened its food systems and supply chains with the assistance from the UN COVID-19 Response and Recovery Fund, the Food and Agriculture Organization (FAO) and the fisheries industry.",""],[1,"69","6","Agriculture Training Programme","This resulted in agriculture training programmes for both genders, efforts to improve soils and the distribution of seeds and planting materials.",""],[1,"69","6","Soil Improvement and Seed Distribution Support","This resulted in agriculture training programmes for both genders, efforts to improve soils and the distribution of seeds and planting materials.",""],[1,"69","7","Integrated Food Security and Resilient Ecosystems Strategy","The overarching strategy to address the issue of food insecurity in Kiribati is to integrate sector- specific approaches and promote healthy and resilient ecosystems through increasing the distribution of food crops for re-planting and animal breeds for cross breeding.",""]],"26":[[1,"6","10","Marine and Coastal Infrastructure Upgrade","upgrading marine and coastal infrastructure",""],[1,"6","10","Road and Runway Improvement Programme","improving roads and runways",""],[1,"6","10","Transportation Services Improvement Programme","improving transportation services",""],[1,"67","13","Infrastructure Project Management Capacity Building","Capacity building of agencies and bodies who have roles in the project management and implementation of infrastructure investments and development projects would critically important.",""]],"27":[[1,"6","6","Renewable Energy Generation Expansion","Increasing the generation of sustainable renewable sources of energy;",""],[1,"6","10","Energy Supply Improvement Programme","improving energy supply in Kiribati",""],[1,"93","8","Annual CSO Support for PUB Operations","the Government provides annual CSOs to help fund PUB's operations",""],[1,"93","8","PUB Infrastructure Maintenance and Refurbishment Funding","along with project funding of around $1.5 million for the maintenance of its generators, refurbishment of electricity distribution and facility clean up.",""],[1,"94","4","Public Utility Board Capacity Expansion","Therefore, to facilitate economic expansion, it is important that we increase the capacity of PUB to meet this growing demand.",""],[1,"95","1","Renewable Energy Investment Programme","we are placing high priority on investment in renewable energy as part of our adaptation programme as outlined in the KIER 2017.",""],[1,"95","4","Solar Power System Centralisation and Expansion","There is potential to increase solar energy access and convert Kiribati to a 100 percent solar-powered country by 2036 through the centralisation of solar power system firstly in the Outer Islands and then in South Tarawa.",""],[1,"95","5","Island Solar PV Electrification Investment","An estimated cost of around $4 million is needed to fully install electricity in each island which would require around $64 million for all the islands in the Gilbert Group to have electricity powered by solar PVs.",""],[1,"95","6","South Tarawa Renewable Energy Project","New projects including the South Tarawa Renewable Energy Project (STREP) and Promoting Outer Island Development through the Integrated Energy Roadmap (POIDIER) project are also underway.",""],[1,"95","6","Outer Island Energy Development through the Integrated Energy Roadmap","New projects including the South Tarawa Renewable Energy Project (STREP) and Promoting Outer Island Development through the Integrated Energy Roadmap (POIDIER) project are also underway.",""]],"28":[[1,"6","10","ICT Development and Data Access Improvement","Improving ICT development and data access",""],[1,"86","13","Digital Connectivity, ICT Development and Data Access Improvement","Improve access to digital connectivity, ICT development and data access.",""],[1,"96","4","ICT Infrastructure Development","This plan will work to ensure that opportunities for ICT infrastructure development are tapped to ensure continued functioning of societies while maintaining physical distancing as may be required to minimize the spread of the deadly virus.",""],[1,"97","5","Submarine Cable Connectivity Project","The answer to most of our challenges regarding digital connectivity will be resolved through the submarine cable project, finance by the ADB and WB respectively.",""],[1,"97","6","Submarine Cable Internet Connectivity Project","the submarine cables will provide faster and better internet quality than satellite dishes",""],[1,"98","1","Outer Islands Backhaul Upgrade for Internet Access","The second component of the submarine cable project is upgrading the backhaul to the Outer Islands through a combination of microwave and satellites.",""],[1,"98","2","Government Wide Area Network Initiative","Complementing the submarine cable project is the local Government Wide Area Network (GWAN) initiative.",""],[1,"98","3","ICT Project Financing and Donor Partnership Support","For the sustainability and consistency of these projects, availability of funds and investments are required.",""],[1,"98","3","Donor Partnership for Technical and Financial Support","Therefore, maintaining the strong partnership with donors are necessary for technical and financial support.",""]],"29":[[1,"80","6","National Standard Database Development and Update","The NSO must develop and update the national standard database ensuring effective implementation by all Ministries to support decision makers in providing accurate and reliable data for transparent reports.",""],[1,"80","7","ICT Strengthening for E-Government Service Delivery","Information, Communication and Technology (ICT) needs to be strengthened to promote the use of available technology and implementation of standard e-Government services such as information services, download and upload services, transaction services, participation and communication services, and to collaborate with the NSO as an integrated, one-stop service/portal.",""],[1,"80","10","Civil Registry Population Register System Strengthening","The Civil Registry Office needs to have a well-established and reliable system for its population register to ensure that all citizens are accounted for in the database to assist policy decisions in social benefits, land ownership, elections and many more.",""],[1,"81","10","Government Coordination and Silo-Reduction Reform","Strengthening common functions across Government, which will include removing silos in Government operations and improving coordination;",""],[1,"81","11","Centralised Customer Service Delivery","Centralising customer service functions for the delivery of efficient and effective customer services;",""],[1,"81","12","Digital Government Roadmap Implementation","Investing and promoting the use of available technology to execute the Digital Government Roadmap, which will include the introduction of e-Government services.",""],[1,"81","13","Government Process Simplification and Automation","Improving, simplifying and automating Government-wide processes, which will include a centralised data service;",""],[1,"98","3","E-Government Project Initiation","These milestones in the ICT sector will facilitate the initiation of e-Government projects to enhance the efficiency and effectiveness of service delivery in the public sector.",""]],"30":[[1,"86","9","Marine and Coastal Infrastructure Improvement and Upgrading","Improve and upgrade marine and coastal infrastructure;",""],[1,"90","22","Marine and Coastal Infrastructure Development Programme","Through this KDP, we aim to build, upgrade and sustain our marine and coastal infrastructure for the benefit of current and future generations.",""],[1,"90","23","Port Upgrading and Construction Programme","Upgrading existing ports and constructing new ones are solutions to improving interisland and international connectivity.",""],[1,"91","1","Outer Islands Shipping and Cargo Transport Improvement","Investment of this type will allow regularity of shipping services and improve the delivery of cargo to the Outer Islands, as well as the uplifting of copra, attendance of emergency cases and transportation of products to both local and international markets.",""],[1,"91","3","Outer Islands Port Upgrade Project","Efforts to tackle the issue of connectivity include a project to upgrade ports in four of the Outer Islands within four years and, later, other remaining islands.",""],[1,"91","4","Regional Transshipment Hub Development","this KDP emphasizes the need to create a major transshipment hub for the region to allow more and bigger vessels to dock and more containers to be transported and stored in port yards.",""],[1,"91","5","Port Development Plan in Poland, Kiritimati Island","There is also a major plan to develop the port in Poland, Kiritimati Island.",""],[1,"91","8","Coastal Reinforcement and Mangrove Planting","To avoid destruction of the land, coastal reinforcements need to be in place.",""],[1,"92","4","Improvement of Regular Shipping Services to Outer Islands","Improving the regularity of shipping services to at least once a month is essential to open the market for fish, coconuts and other products from the Outer Islands.",""]],"31":[[1,"6","10","Safe Buildings Improvement Programme","providing safe buildings",""]],"32":[[1,"41","7","Integrated Fisheries Information Management System","Establishment of an integrated fisheries information management system to strengthen fishery and catch management data; funding secured and warrant released for the purchase of the database.",""],[1,"41","21","National Strategy for the Development of Statistics","Enhance the collection and availability of statistics through the implementation of a National Strategy for the Development of Statistics",""]],"33":[[1,"41","20","State-Owned Enterprise Commercialization Reform","Place State Owned Enterprises on a more commercial footing",""],[1,"43","19","State-Owned Enterprises Act Review and Enforcement","Review and better enforcement of the SOE Act;",""],[1,"44","1","State-Owned Enterprise Commercialisation Reforms","Organisational reforms to put SOEs on a more commercial footing.",""],[1,"48","5","State-Owned Enterprise Financial Position Improvement","A solution to this is to improve the financial position of SOEs, thus increasing payments of SOE dividends and decreasing their dependence on CSOs.",""],[1,"48","10","State-Owned Enterprise Dividend Policy","Developing and implementing a dividend policy to ensure compliance by SOEs.",""],[1,"65","15","Subsidy Act Amendment Cabinet Paper","to develop Cabinet paper to amend this Act.",""]],"34":[[1,"3","3","State Capacity and Good Governance Strengthening","The core priorities of the KDP are to eliminate poverty and reduce inequality and injustice through inclusive economic growth, building human capabilities, enhancing the capacity of the state, and strengthening the institutions of good governance and democracy.",""],[1,"6","8","Legal Sector and Institutional Strengthening","improving and strengthening legal sectors and institutions",""],[1,"6","8","Accountability and Transparency Strengthening","strengthening accountability and transparency",""],[1,"6","8","Service Delivery Improvement Programme","change programme to improve service delivery",""],[1,"6","8","Good Governance Advocacy and Promotion","promoting and advocating good governance",""],[1,"16","1","Full Implementation of the Kiribati Development Plan","We, the undersigned, cognitive of our pivotal roles as Heads of Government Ministries, make a collective commitment to fully implement this KDP to the best of our abilities.",""],[1,"22","22","Leadership, Productivity, and Accountability Improvement Initiative","We understand that to be able to 'do more with the same', we must create an enabling climate of leadership at all levels, raise productivity and strengthen accountability.",""],[1,"35","16","Professional Ethics and Standards Programme","Developing and implementing programmes on professional ethics and standards, while transforming mindsets and culture to achieve high standards of performance;",""],[1,"35","17","Performance Assessment and Service Excellence Awards Scheme","Implementing performance assessments with service excellence awards as incentives to higher performance.",""]],"35":[[1,"35","4","Recruiting Agency Operations and Compliance Oversight","Through its Work Relations Unit, the Labour Division also manages the operations and compliance of registered recruiting agencies, including South Pacific Marine Services (SPMS) that employs the bulk of MTC graduates.",""]],"36":[[1,"49","6","Copra Subsidy Scheme","The copra subsidy scheme plays an important part in this national effort.",""],[1,"50","1","Copra Cutter Registration and Incentive Scheme","The Government plans to register all copra cutters in the Outer Islands as being self-employed and provide them with incentives so that the SFU better reaches its intended beneficiaries.",""]],"37":[[1,"19","6","National Behaviour Change Initiative","Behaviour change is therefore one of the top national priorities to strengthen the national commitments towards achieving assigned tasks and responsibilities.",""],[1,"55","8","Community Awareness Programmes","the solution lies in the implementation of more effective community awareness programmes.",""],[1,"55","9","Review of Awareness Programmes and Development of Behavioral Incentives","There is a need to review past awareness programmes in Kiribati and develop innovative incentives to change the behaviors and lifestyles of the general population.",""],[1,"56","1","Review and Strengthen Community-Based Programmes","Review the design and implementation of community-based programmes and involve all relevant stakeholders, including political leaders, community leaders and churches;",""],[1,"56","3","Monitoring of Awareness and Education Programme Effectiveness","Regularly measure the effectiveness of awareness and education programmes, for example reductions in child mortality and NCDs, and strengthen the accountability of these responsibilities.",""],[1,"58","5","Review and Improve Awareness Programmes","Collaborate with MHMS, other Government Departments and NGOs to thoroughly review existing awareness programmes and make them more effective;","MHMS | other Government Departments | NGOs"]],"38":[[1,"55","11","Community Awareness Programmes on Health and Sanitation","Strengthen community awareness programmes on sanitation, neo-natal care, reproductive controls and healthier lifestyles;",""]],"39":[[1,"6","3","Health Monitoring Benchmark Adoption","Adopt international benchmarks as targets to measure achievement regularly",""]],"40":[[1,"76","12","Local Council Officer Training Programme","Increased training for Local council officers",""],[1,"76","15","National Cooperative Policy Development","Development of a National Cooperative Policy to strengthen cooperatives and credit unions.",""],[1,"80","12","Tripartite Decent Work Advisory Board","The tripartite Decent Work Advisory Board (DWAB) plays a crucial advisory role in terms of labour related matters including ILO conventions and labour law reviews.",""]],"41":[[1,"77","12","Provision of Additional Courts for Remote Islands","There is therefore a need for the provision of additional courts to cater for remote islands and inhabited islets, for example, Bikati in Butaritari,and Ribono and Nuotaea on Abaiang.",""],[1,"80","8","Public Complaints Investigation and Prosecution Procedure Reform","The KPS must improve and update policies and procedures in relation to the investigation and prosecution of public complaints to fulfill the public's expectations and ensure it follows professional standards to manage internal affairs in order to bring justice and peace to the people.",""]],"42":[[1,"78","7","Police Accountability and Internal Affairs Management","the Kiribati Police Services (KPS) must be able to fulfill the public's expectations and follow professional standards to manage internal affairs in order to bring justice and peace to the people.",""],[1,"78","11","KPS Equipment and Capacity Strengthening","The increasing number of pending cases also clearly states the need to strengthen the KPS' equipment and capacity to effectively carry out investigations and prosecution of cases.",""]],"43":[[1,"80","11","Border Control Agency Strengthening","As such, strengthening existing border control agencies is a must.",""]],"44":[[1,"70","4","Healthy Lifestyles Awareness Programme","Strengthening awareness programmes on healthy lifestyles and living;",""]]}});